# Optional .gitignore for .mallet/ — copy to <repo>/.mallet/.gitignore by hand.
#
# Mallet does NOT install this. Whether .mallet/ is tracked at all is your
# decision; this template only helps if you have decided to COMMIT .mallet/ and
# want the transient parts left out of history.
#
# If instead you want .mallet/ ignored everywhere on this machine, add
# `.mallet/` to ~/.config/git/ignore (or whatever core.excludesFile points at)
# and do not use this file.

# Transient — regenerated on demand, no value in history
pipeline-state/
compact-snapshot.md

# Point-in-time snapshots — commit deliberately with `git add -f` if wanted
discovery-*.md

# Session-scoped working state
missions/
task-notes.md

# Durable and worth committing, listed here only as documentation:
#   conventions.md      project conventions
#   memory.md           persistent project facts
#   lessons.md          recorded corrections
#   skill-backlog.md    candidate skills
#   overrides/          per-skill amendments
#   skills/             project-specific skills
#   features/           feature plans
